.TH CDCSTORE-MOUNT 1 "October 2026" "cdcstore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdcstore\-mount \- mount a cdcstore repository read\-only (FUSE)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdcstore\-mount
[\-f] [\-d] [\-o OPTION,...] REPO MOUNTPOINT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mounts a repository as a read\-only folder. The files appear with their stored paths, modes, times and links. A read fetches only the chunk files it touches. All chunk files must be present; a missing one makes the read fail with an error instead of returning wrong bytes. Nothing is cached or decoded: the repository is plain files.
.PP
REPO is a repository folder, or a folder that holds .cdcstore. Unmount with fusermount3 \-u MOUNTPOINT. Needs libfuse3.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Stay in the foreground; errors are printed to the terminal.
.TP
.B \-d
Foreground, plus libfuse debug output.
.TP
.B \-o OPT,...
Mount options passed to libfuse, such as allow_other.
